A medical kit wedged under the rock, where the dust would not find it.


// ---- People: someone you can walk up to and talk with. `Calm: yes` means they never
// attack. `Talk scene:` is the scene a click on them opens. `Face:` is shown beside what
// they say (`male`, `female`, or a face string).
## [People](people)

### [Old Marrow](marrow)
---
Area: landing
Mark: caretaker
Sprite: fig:junker_m
Face: male
Calm: yes
Talk scene: marrow
Scan: One human. Elevated pulse, and a wet cough.
---
The relay's caretaker, sitting on an upturned crate beside his tent.

// ---- Lecture 11.
### [Pim](pim)
---
Area: gully
Mark: camp
Sprite: fig:junker_f
Face: female
Calm: yes
Talk scene: pim
Scan: One human, young. Cold, and not hurt.
---
Marrow's apprentice, wrapped in a survey blanket with her back to a rock.

// Pim again, by the tent. She is not on the map until a scene sends for her:
// `; summon pim_yard`.
### [Pim](pim_yard)
---
Area: landing
At: 11, 4
Sprite: fig:junker_f
Face: female
Calm: yes
Talk scene: pim_yard
Hidden until: pim_went_home
---
Marrow's apprentice, home, with a mug in both hands.


// ---- Hostiles: someone who walks a `Patrol:` (cells, `x y; x y`), notices a crew member
// within `Notice:` cells, and attacks. `HP:` is how much it takes; `Stun:` how many
// seconds a stun shot holds it; `Drops:` what it leaves where it falls.
## [Hostiles](hostiles)

### [Relay sentry](sentry)
---
Area: landing
Mark: sentry
Sprite: fig:robot_war
HP: 2
Damage: 1
Notice: 4
Stun: 10
Speed: 2
Patrol: 18 9; 27 9; 27 11; 18 11
Drops: power_cell
Scan: Security frame, nine days without a recognition update. One power cell.
---
A security frame walking the same square it has walked for nine days.

// ---- Lecture 11. A hostile is a person without `Calm: yes`.
### [Sump crawler](crawler)
---
Area: cistern
At: 13, 3
Sprite: fig:glassback
HP: 3
Damage: 1
Notice: 3
Stun: 8
Speed: 2
Patrol: 12 1; 13 5; 12 5; 13 1
Drops: tablet
Scan: Silicate shell, about the size of a dog. It has something flat in its jaws.
---
Something low and glassy that has had the walkway to itself for nine days.


// ---- Scenes: what is said, and what can be answered. Each `%` line is something the
// scene may say (one is picked). Each `-` line is a choice: `[words](where it leads)`,
// then `if <who may take it>`, then `; <what it does>`. An empty `()` ends the scene.
//
// WHO: a job (`if medical`), how good (`if skill science >= 3`), what they carry
// (`if holding power_cell`), or what the party has worked out - how many things
// (`if learned >= 2`) or one named thing (`if learned codes`).
//
// WHAT IT DOES: `learn <fact>`, `signal <name>`, `take <item>`, `give <item>`,
// `check <skill> <number> else <scene>` (a failed roll goes to that scene instead),
// `completes <quest>`, `fails <quest>`.
## [Scenes](scenes)

### [The Yard Terminal](terminal)
%{learned codes < 1} One line on the screen, over and over: DOOR SEALED. AWAITING CODE.
%{learned codes} DOOR SEALED. AWAITING CODE. And now you have one to give it.

- [Read the log](terminal_log) ; learn log
- [Pull the door code out of its memory](terminal_code) if skill science >= 3
- [Force the service port](terminal_code) ; check engineering 8 else terminal_dead
- [Send the door code](terminal_sent) if learned codes ; signal relay_unlocked
- [Send the sentry its recognition update](terminal_update) if learned codes ; calm sentry
- [Play back the last call it sent](terminal_call) if comms ; signal last_call_heard
- [Step back]()

### [Recognition Update](terminal_update)
% The terminal sends nine days of crew lists in one burst. Out in the yard the sentry stops, turns its head toward you, and goes back to its square with its weapon down.

- [Step back]()

### [The Last Call](terminal_call)
% One call, nine days old, to a convoy tender that never answered: CELL FAILING. SEND A SPARE. The relay asked for help once, and then saved its power.

- [Step back](terminal)

### [Nine Days](terminal_log)
% Day one: beacon cell failing. Day two: cell removed for test and fitted to the sentry, which has the only good socket. Day three: sentry no longer answers to its keeper. The entries stop.

- [Step back](terminal)

### [Six Digits](terminal_code)
% The door code is six digits, stored in the clear. Whoever built this place trusted the dust to keep people out.

- [Copy it down](terminal) ; learn codes

### [Dead Screen](terminal_dead)
% The service port spits once and the screen goes dark. The log, the code and the cursor go with it.

- [Step back]()

### [The Door Answers](terminal_sent)
% The terminal thinks about it. Across the yard, the relay door drops its bolts with a bang.

- [Step back]()

### [Old Marrow](marrow)
% "Nine days dark. I kept the kettle on and nobody came." He coughs into his sleeve, and looks at your uniform as if it might not be real.

- [Ask how to get into the relay house](marrow_key)
- [Ask about the sentry](marrow_sentry)
- [Ask what he has put by](marrow_cache) ; signal cache_known
- [Show him the brass key](marrow_pump) if party pump_house_key
- [Ask where a shuttle could set down](marrow_strip) if helm ; signal strip_found
- [Look at that cough](marrow_treated) if medical ; signal marrow_treated
- [Leave him to his kettle]()

### [The Brass Key](marrow_pump)
% "That is the pump house. Pim went out there the day the beacon failed, to start the pump, and I have not had the legs to go and look for her." He closes your fingers over the key.

- [Ask him something else](marrow)
- [Thank him]()

### [The Old Strip](marrow_strip)
% "South of the pad, where the scrub is flat. The supply boats used it before my time." He looks pleased that somebody asked.

- [Ask him something else](marrow)
- [Thank him]()

### [The Keycard](marrow_key)
% "Keycard. I dropped it in the yard the day the sentry turned on me, and I have not been back for it. The terminal by the door knows the code too, if you can make it talk."

- [Ask him something else](marrow)
- [Thank him]()

### [The Sentry](marrow_sentry)
% "It has the beacon's power cell in its chest. Stun it and you have ten seconds. Put it down for good and the cell is yours - and the beacon wants one."

- [Ask him something else](marrow)
- [Thank him]()

### [Put By](marrow_cache)
% He nods at the scrub beside the landing pad. "Medical kit, under the netting. I was saving it for somebody worse off than me. That might be you, if you go near the sentry."

- [Ask him something else](marrow)
- [Thank him]()

### [Dust Lung](marrow_treated)
% You listen to his chest for a long minute. Dust lung, nine days of it, and nothing that will not mend. He takes the inhaler like it is made of glass.

- [Leave him to his kettle]()

// THE ENDINGS. Both `Call it in` answers complete the quest `relight`, which has a
// `Win:` line - that wins the game. `Step back from the smoke` fails it, and it has a
// `Lose:` line - that loses it. Either way the landing party is brought home.
### [The Beacon](beacon)
% The beacon fills the room, dark. The socket for its power cell is empty, and somebody has left the governor housing open.

- [Fit the power cell](beacon_lit) if holding power_cell ; take power_cell
- [Bring it up by hand on the standby coil](beacon_hand) if engineering ; check engineering 11 else beacon_burn
- [Pull the governor and run it wide open](beacon_burn)
- [Leave it dark for now]()

### [Light](beacon_lit)
% The cell seats with a click you feel in your teeth. The lamp turns once, twice, and then the whole room is white.

- [Call it in]() ; completes relight

### [Light, the Hard Way](beacon_hand)
% The standby coil whines, catches and holds. It is not pretty, and it will not last a year. It will last until somebody brings a new cell.

- [Call it in]() ; completes relight

### [Smoke](beacon_burn)
% The coil arcs white, then orange, then nothing at all. What is left of the lamp is glass on the floor and a smell you will not forget.

- [Step back from the smoke]() ; fails relight


// ---- Lecture 10: what the new props open.
### [The Notice](notice)
% SPARE BEACON CELL KEPT BELOW, IN THE COLD. DRAIN THE TANK FIRST. The paper comes apart in your fingers as you read the last line.

- [Let the pieces fall]() ; learn spare

### [The Pump Panel](pump_panel)
%{party fuse < 3} Three fuse clips, all empty. The lever will not do anything until they are full.
%{party fuse >= 3} Three fuse clips, all empty, and three fuses between you.

- [Fit three fuses and throw the lever](pump_run) if holding fuse >= 3 ; take fuse 3
- [Fit two, and bridge the third clip with wire](pump_run) if holding fuse >= 2 ; take fuse 2, check engineering 10 else pump_spark
- [Jam a crowbar across all three clips](pump_burn)
- [Leave it alone]()

### [The Pump Runs](pump_run)
% The pump coughs, catches, and settles to a hammering you can feel through the floor. Somewhere under your feet, a great deal of water starts to move.

- [Step back]() ; signal cistern_drained

### [A Bright Blue Spark](pump_spark)
% The wire glows, sags and parts, and two good fuses go with it. Nothing else happens, and you have burned your thumb.

- [Step back]()

### [Fire in the Pump House](pump_burn)
% The crowbar welds itself to the clips. The panel burns first, then the cable under it, and that cable runs all the way back to the relay house.

- [Run]() ; fails relight


// ---- Lecture 11: somebody to talk to.
### [Pim](pim)
% "You are from the ship." She does not get up. "I came out here to start the pump, nine days ago. I got as far as the door."

- [Ask what stopped her](pim_why)
- [Ask about the spare cell](pim_spare) if learned spare
- [Ask if she has anything for a fight](pim_stash) ; reveal stash
- [Give her the tablet](pim_thanks) if holding tablet ; take tablet, completes pim_tablet, give fuse
- [Tell her the tablet is yours now](pim_angry) if holding tablet ; rouse pim, fails pim_tablet
- [Leave her be]()

### [What Stopped Her](pim_why)
% "There is something on the walkway down there. It took my tablet out of my hand and I ran. I have been working up to going back for it ever since."

- [Promise to bring it back](pim) ; accepts pim_tablet
- [Ask her something else](pim)
- [Leave her be]()

### [Below](pim_spare)
% "The spare. Yes. It is in the tank room, past the sluice, and the sluice will not move until the tank is dry." She draws the stairs for you in the dust, and where they come out.

- [Ask her something else](pim)
- [Leave her be]()

### [Under the Rock](pim_stash)
% She tips her head at the rock behind her. "Medical kit. Marrow packs one for me every time, and I never open it."

- [Ask her something else](pim)
- [Leave her be]()

### [Nine Days of Readings](pim_thanks)
% She turns the tablet over twice before she believes it. Then she takes a fuse out of her lamp and puts it in your hand. "I will not need the light. I am going home."

- [Watch her go]() ; dismiss pim, summon pim_yard

### [Yours Now](pim_angry)
% She is on her feet before you have finished the sentence, and there is a cutting torch in her hand that was not there a moment ago.

- [Back away]()

### [Pim, at Home](pim_yard)
% "Marrow says I am to thank you properly." She holds up a small gray remote. "I wired the relay house door to this years ago, so I would never need his keycard."

- [Ask her to open the relay house](pim_remote) ; open door
- [Leave her to her tea]()

### [The Remote](pim_remote)
% She points it over her shoulder without looking. Across the yard the relay door drops its bolts.

- [Thank her]()
